; The JSON rendering of every answer the tool gives — one module, so that the
; command line and the MCP server emit the same object for the same question
; and neither can drift from the other. It depends on the engine and on the
; JSON value type, and on nothing with I/O: it turns values into a [Json.t],
; and whoever asked prints it.
;
; Its own library rather than a module of [writ_runtime], because the runtime
; depends on [writ_data] ONLY and that is a layering the build enforces; and
; not a module of [writ_cli], because the MCP server wants it too and must not
; link the command line to get it. UNWRAPPED, as its neighbours are, so the
; module is [Report_json] and nothing else.

(library
 (name writ_report_json)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries writ_data writ_runtime writ_json))
